{# ===========================================================================
   Component: location-gallery

   The room gallery for a location page. Real photography of this room, which
   is section 1 of the location page template in SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md and the
   thing every stub page is still missing.

   USAGE
     {% set gallery = roomPhotos[loc.id] %}
     {% if gallery %}{% include "components/location-gallery.njk" %}{% endif %}

   Expects `gallery` (a roomPhotos entry) and `loc` (a locations.json item) in
   scope. Renders nothing at all if `gallery` is undefined, which is the case
   for every location whose photography has not been curated yet. That gate is
   the point: an empty gallery frame reads as a broken page, and a missing
   section reads as a page that simply does not have that section.

   Photography comes from roomPhotos.js, which throws at build time if a file
   is missing from the manifest or still carries the generator's draft alt
   text. So there is no fallback branch here for a missing alt: it cannot get
   this far.

   Reuses .bento, .cell and .shot from interior.css and location.css rather
   than introducing a gallery of its own, per CLAUDE.md: never hand-build
   markup a component covers.

   No lazy loading on the first image. It is the largest element above the
   fold on a location page and lazy-loading it costs LCP directly.
   =========================================================================== #}

{#- galleryId keeps the heading id unique when a page renders this component
    more than once. A location page shows rooms AND dishes as two separate
    calls, and two sections both claiming id="room-title" would make
    aria-labelledby resolve to whichever the parser saw first. -#}
{%- set gId = galleryId | default("room-title") %}
<section class="sect sect--alt sect--rule" aria-labelledby="{{ gId }}">
  <div class="sect__inner">
    <header class="sect__head">
      {#- Defaults to "The room" for a single location. Overridable for a
          caller showing more than one, where the singular would read wrong. -#}
      <span class="sect__eyebrow">{{ galleryEyebrow | default("The room") }}</span>
      <h2 class="sect__title" id="{{ gId }}">{{ galleryTitle | safe }}</h2>
      {%- if galleryNote %}
      <p class="sect__note">{{ galleryNote | safe }}</p>
      {%- endif %}
    </header>

    <div class="bento">
      {%- for shot in gallerySet %}
      <figure class="cell shot{% if shot.wide %} shot--wide{% endif %} reveal">
        <img
          class="shot__img"
          src="{{ shot.src }}"
          alt="{{ shot.alt }}"
          loading="lazy"
          width="{{ shot.width }}"
          height="{{ shot.height }}">
        <figcaption class="shot__caption">
          <span class="shot__name">{{ shot.caption }}</span>
          {%- if shot.tag %}<span class="shot__tag">{{ shot.tag }}</span>{% endif %}
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
